      "body": "## Summary\n\nPartial fix for #19612: Align `SGLANG_JIT_CACHE_DIR` with the unified `SGLANG_CACHE_DIR` root.\n\n### Problem\n\nSGLang already directs third-party JIT caches (Triton, Inductor, CUDA, TileLang, FlashInfer) under `SGLANG_CACHE_DIR` via `redirect_third_party_caches()`, and other internal caches (`SGLANG_DG_CACHE_DIR`, `SGLANG_CUTE_AOT_CACHE_DIR`) resolve relative to it using `_default_cache_subdir()`. However, `SGLANG_JIT_CACHE_DIR` was inconsistent:\n\n- **`environ.py`**: declared as `EnvStr(None)` (no default)\n- **`cache.py`**: hardcoded fallback `\"~/.cache/sglang/jit\"`\n\nThis split meant setting `SGLANG_CACHE_DIR=/mnt/cache` did **not** redirect the JIT kernel build cache — operators needed a separate `SGLANG_JIT_CACHE_DIR=/mnt/cache/jit` override.\n\n### Fix\n\n1. **`environ.py`** — Changed `SGLANG_JIT_CACHE_DIR` from `EnvStr(None)` to `EnvStr(lambda: _default_cache_subdir(\"jit\"))`, matching the pattern used by `SGLANG_DG_CACHE_DIR` and `SGLANG_CUTE_AOT_CACHE_DIR`.\n\n2. **`cache.py`** — Updated `cache_root()` fallback from a hardcoded `\"~/.cache/sglang/jit\"` to `os.path.join(os.path.expanduser(envs.SGLANG_CACHE_DIR.get()), \"jit\")`, eliminating the second source of truth.\n\n### Result\n\nAll JIT/precompilation caches now resolve under a single configurable root:\n\n| Cache | Default path | Override env |\n|-------|-------------|--------------|\n| Triton | `$SGLANG_CACHE_DIR/triton` | `TRITON_CACHE_DIR` |\n| Inductor | `$SGLANG_CACHE_DIR/inductor` | `TORCHINDUCTOR_CACHE_DIR` |\n| CUDA | `$SGLANG_CACHE_DIR/nv` | `CUDA_CACHE_PATH` |\n| TileLang | `$SGLANG_CACHE_DIR/tilelang` | `TILELANG_CACHE_DIR` |\n| FlashInfer | `$SGLANG_CACHE_DIR` base | `FLASHINFER_WORKSPACE_BASE` |\n| DeepGEMM | `$SGLANG_CACHE_DIR/deep_gemm` | `SGLANG_DG_CACHE_DIR` |\n| CuTe AOT | `$SGLANG_CACHE_DIR/cute_aot` | `SGLANG_CUTE_AOT_CACHE_DIR` |\n| **JIT kernel builds** | `$SGLANG_CACHE_DIR/jit` | `SGLANG_JIT_CACHE_DIR` |\n\nSetting `SGLANG_CACHE_DIR=/mnt/cache/sglang` now redirects every cache at once.\n\n### Backward Compatibility\n\n- If `SGLANG_JIT_CACHE_DIR` is explicitly set, it still takes precedence\n- Default path changes from `None` → `~/.cache/sglang/jit` (same as `cache.py`'s previous hardcoded fallback)\n- External callers that read `SGLANG_JIT_CACHE_DIR` will now see a concrete path when unset instead of `None`\n\n---\n\nRefs: #19612\n\nSigned-off-by: yancy <yancy@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #38407097560](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38407097560)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #38407096687](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38407096687)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #38407097015](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38407097015)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
